WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:07.439
Speaker 1: I want to talk about a story in
which a daughter whose dad recently died of

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:15.679
covid went on CNN and at least partially blamed
Fox News propagandist Tucker Carlson for his

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:23.640
role in her dad's covid death, her dad falling
for misinformation, including the misinformation

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.310
he consumed from Tucker Carlson.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.420
And they're sort of like three stories here.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:36.350
One is to what degree, if any, does Tucker
do other media people bear responsibility

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.100
for these deaths?

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.989
Number two, is there something that feels
a little bit off or exploitative about these

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:47.680
types of interviews with the surviving family
members?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.309
And then number three, something a bunch of
people emailed me about, which is could there

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:59.350
ever be like a legal responsibility for someone
in the media as a result of people that die

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.390
thanks to having followed or fallen for that
misinformation?

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:09.210
So to set the stage just briefly, this article
outlines what happened here.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:14.840
Daughter blames Tucker Carlson's misinformation
for playing a role in Dad's covid death.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.400
The 45 year old father of two had no underlying
health conditions.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:25.260
A Washington woman whose father died of the
coronavirus said he was hesitant to get vaccinated

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:30.690
because of misinformation he heard in right
wing media and specifically cited Fox News

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.860
host Tucker Carlson.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:37.180
Katie Lane said her father, 45 year old Boeing
designer Patrick Lane, wasn't on the far right

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:38.180
politically.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.010
We'll get to that.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:45.370
When asked what specifically made her father
refuse the shot, the 20 year old cited Tucker

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.180
Carlson.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.250
Katie said her father was waiting for full
FDA approval before getting the shot.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:55.000
And this is interesting, but by the time that
happened, he was already sick.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.560
One of his last comments was he wished he
had been vaccinated.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.350
And there have been many, many people saying,
I'm just waiting for that full approval, that

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:06.070
full approval has come and gone and many still
not interested in getting vaccinated.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.450
For Patrick Lane, it was too late.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.450
He was, too.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.450
He was already sick.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.739
He couldn't get vaccinated.

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:13.340
Let's listen to some of the interview and
then discuss.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:17.489
Speaker 2: Why was he so hesitant to get vaccinated?

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:18.730
Katie?

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:26.769
Speaker 3: There there's multiple reasons,
I think one of which was some of the media

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:31.260
that he ingested, he wasn't by any means far
right.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.940
He was right in the middle and he consumed
media from both sides.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:41.900
And just some of the misinformation on one
of those sides made him hesitant.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.660
So he was going to wait for FDA approval.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:48.690
But by the time that Pfizer had been approved,
it was already too late.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.359
Speaker 2: Pfizer got the full FDA approval
and your father was already sick.

00:02:53.359 --> 00:02:58.060
Evan, talk to me about.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.290
Your final goodbye to your father, did you
have a chance to spend any real time with

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:03.290
him?

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:08.049
Speaker 1: So this is the part that to me
is starting to feel a little bit exploitative.

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:13.409
I've seen a bunch of interviews like this
and and there's a disaster porn aspect to

00:03:13.409 --> 00:03:14.409
it.

00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:18.770
I'm not feeling fully comfortable with it,
including the desire to figure out what were

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.019
the last words.

00:03:20.019 --> 00:03:22.420
And you'll see that at a point soon.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.660
John Berman actually asks, were those his
last words?

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:29.919
And I think it's it's the daughter says, well,
those were his last words to my step mom or

00:03:29.919 --> 00:03:30.919
something like that.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:36.430
But there's something that's starting to almost
get, like, salacious about these interviews.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:38.129
I don't know that I'm loving it.

00:03:38.129 --> 00:03:39.730
Speaker 4: Not really.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:46.069
I was already staying at another house and
he was just coming by to pick something up.

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:52.730
And he didn't even want to get too close because
he was too worried about getting me sick.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:58.900
So I didn't get to hug him before he left
and then before I knew he was gone.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:04.709
Speaker 2: You guys are vaccinated now, Evan,
what was the message ultimately that your

00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:07.409
father wanted to spread about vaccines?

00:04:07.409 --> 00:04:11.930
Speaker 4: He wasn't.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:20.230
Anti vaccine, he was just hesitant and I know
that, you know, Pfizer has been FDA approved.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:24.259
I don't think he would have anything wrong
with telling people to get that vaccine.

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:30.610
Speaker 3: Yeah, his final words to my step
mom on a FaceTime call was that he wishes

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:32.449
he wished that he was vaccinated.

00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:35.470
Speaker 2: Those were his final words.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:42.860
Speaker 3: To my step mom, I the last call
that she had with him, he said that he wished

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.880
that he was vaccinated.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:47.569
Speaker 1: So like, what are people with me?

00:04:47.569 --> 00:04:49.750
Does this feel somewhat exploitative?

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:54.610
Like I mean, if maybe if the point is just
to convince people to get vaccinated, maybe

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:55.770
this is effective.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.770
I just don't know.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:57.770
I'm not sure.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:03.919
Speaker 2: And, Candy, you said from one media
source in particular, he was getting misinformation.

00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:07.300
He was getting information that led him to
be hesitant on vaccines.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.070
Who I mean, who was he listening to?

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:18.610
Speaker 3: He he watched some Tucker Carlson
videos on YouTube and some of those videos

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:23.919
involved some misinformation about vaccines,
and I believe that that played a role.

00:05:23.919 --> 00:05:27.169
Speaker 2: Evan, what do you want
Speaker 1: people to remember?

00:05:27.169 --> 00:05:29.879
So where where to even start?

00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:30.879
Right.

00:05:30.879 --> 00:05:35.940
I got an email asking more or less about legal
liability, like if you can demonstrate that

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:40.250
this guy wasn't vaccinated because if Tucker
Carlson, could there be legal liability?

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.759
No, absolutely not.

00:05:41.759 --> 00:05:43.909
I mean, you even if in theory.

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:47.050
So let's see where there's multiple reasons
as to why not.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:56.110
First of all, how do you you'd have to demonstrate
that no one, were it not only for Tucker Carlson,

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:58.360
this man would have been vaccinated.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:03.169
The vaccine is not 100 percent effective at
preventing death.

00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:06.330
It's very effective at preventing death, but
not 100, 100 percent.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:10.550
So you could not even prove that had this
particular person been vaccinated, they would

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.720
not have died.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:19.300
But moreover, you know, Fox News has already
argued legally that Tucker Carlson shows entertainment,

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:26.780
that no reasonable person would would interpret
what Tucker says as fact, that it's performative,

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.919
that it's entertainment.

00:06:28.919 --> 00:06:35.620
And also there are so many instances and so
many media outlets where disinformation is

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:40.350
being spread, whether it's called entertainment
or news.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.880
There's no there's not going to be it would
never succeed to try to hold Tucker.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.979
Tucker Carlson, legally liable for this.

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:53.970
So I guess the questions are given that it's
undeniable that the misinformation does play

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.280
a role in people not getting vaccinated.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.560
What could be done?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.020
What should be done from a legal standpoint,
if anything, or is it just a matter of this

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.889
is just speech and certainly platforms can
regulate it if they want.

00:07:06.889 --> 00:07:12.400
Facebook can say we will police disinformation
content about vaccines.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.789
But that's not a legal issue.

00:07:13.789 --> 00:07:14.789
It's not illegal.

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:17.781
It's just Facebook says, well, we're not going
to allow it on our platform, which is their

00:07:17.781 --> 00:07:19.290
right to do.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:24.789
And then lastly, how are people feeling about
these types of segments in general?

00:07:24.789 --> 00:07:28.770
The what were the last words and this type
of thing?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.490
Is there an exploitative aspect to it?

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:38.550
Is there an exploitative aspect that's acceptable
if the goal is to convince people to get vaccinated?

00:07:38.550 --> 00:08:18.849
Let me know what 

00:08:18.849 --> 00:08:44.680
you think.

